d ZIP files as ZIP files"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-1796", "fix_versions": ["26.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-1703", "GHSA-6vgw-5pg2-w6jp"], "description": "pip Path Traversal vulnerability"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-2876", "fix_versions": ["26.1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jp4c-xjxw-mgf9", "CVE-2026-6357"], "description": "pip Vulnerable to Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-3721", "fix_versions": ["26.2.0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qwm4-qh6w-59xr", "CVE-2026-13346"], "description": "pip would incorrectly handle doubly-encoded package URLs from indexes"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-196", "fix_versions": ["26.1.2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-8643", "GHSA-wf93-45jw-7689"], "description": " pip: Path traversal in console_scripts/gui_scripts\u00a0entry point names allows installing scripts outside of target directory"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-1795", "fix_versions": ["25.3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4xh5-x5gv-qwph", "CVE-2025-8869"], "description": "pip's fallback tar extraction doesn't check symbolic links point to extraction directory"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-1796", "fix_versions": ["26.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-1703", "GHSA-6vgw-5pg2-w6jp"], "description": "pip Path Traversal vulnerability"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-196", "fix_versions": ["26.1.2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-8643", "GHSA-wf93-45jw-7689"], "description": "pip would treat console_scripts and gui_scripts as paths instead of file names without sanitizing the resolved absolute path to the installation directory, leading to entry points being installed outside the installation directory."}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-2875", "fix_versions": ["26.1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-58qw-9mgm-455v", "CVE-2026-3219"], "description": "pip has an interpretation conflict due to handling both concatenated tar and ZIP files as ZIP files"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-2876", "fix_versions": ["26.1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jp4c-xjxw-mgf9", "CVE-2026-6357"], "description": "pip Vulnerable to Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-3721", "fix_versions": ["26.2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qwm4-qh6w-59xr", "CVE-2026-13346"], "description": "pip would incorrectly handle doubly-encoded package URLs from indexes allowing for files to be installed to arbitrary locations on disk even when installing wheels.     This vulnerability requires downloading or installing a package from a malicious package index to succeed, malicious packages alone are not able to exploit this vulnerability. Note that this vulnerability only materially impacts users running `pip download` with the `--only-binary` option as installing source distributions from an untrusted index is already an unsafe operation that executes code during install time."}]}, {"name": "platformdirs", "version": "4.9.4", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pluggy", "version": "1.6.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "py-key-value-aio", "version": "0.4.4", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pycparser", "version": "3.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pydantic", "version": "2.12.5", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pydantic-settings", "version": "2.15.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pydantic-core", "version": "2.41.5", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pygments", "version": "2.21.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pyjwt", "version": "2.15.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pyperclip", "version": "1.11.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pytest", "version": "9.0.3", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pytest-asyncio", "version": "1.3.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pytest-cov", "version": "7.1.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "python-dotenv", "version": "1.2.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "python-multipart", "version": "0.0.32", "vulns": []}, {"name": "pyyaml", "version": "6.0.3", "vulns": []}, {"name": "referencing", "version": "0.37.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "regex", "version": "2026.5.9", "vulns": []}, {"name": "respx", "version": "0.23.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "rich", "version": "14.3.3", "vulns": []}, {"name": "rich-rst", "version": "1.3.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "rpds-py", "version": "0.30.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "safetensors", "version": "0.8.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "scikit-learn", "version": "1.9.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "scipy", "version": "1.18.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "secretstorage", "version": "3.5.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "sentence-transformers", "version": "5.6.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "setuptools", "version": "78.1.0", "vulns": [{"id": "PYSEC-2025-49", "fix_versions": ["78.1.1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5rjg-fvgr-3xxf", "BIT-setuptools-2025-47273", "CVE-2025-47273"], "description": "setuptools has a path traversal vulnerability in PackageIndex.download that leads to Arbitrary File Write"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-3447", "fix_versions": ["83.0.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-59890", "BIT-setuptools-2026-59890", "GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c"], "description": "setuptools: MANIFEST.in exclusion bypass in sdist via Unicode normalization collision (NFC/NFD) on macOS APFS/HFS+"}, {"id": "PYSEC-2025-49", "fix_versions": ["78.1.1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5rjg-fvgr-3xxf", "CVE-2025-47273", "BIT-setuptools-2025-47273"], "description": "setuptools is a package that allows users to download, build, install, upgrade, and uninstall Python packages. A path traversal vulnerability in `PackageIndex` is present in setuptools prior to version 78.1.1. An attacker would be allowed to write files to arbitrary locations on the filesystem with the permissions of the process running the Python code, which could escalate to remote code execution depending on the context. Version 78.1.1 fixes the issue."}, {"id": "PYSEC-2026-3447", "fix_versions": ["83.0.0"], "aliases": ["BIT-setuptools-2026-59890", "GHSA-h35f-9h28-mq5c", "CVE-2026-59890"], "description": "setuptools is a package that allows users to download, build, install, upgrade, and uninstall Python packages. Prior to 83.0.0, FileList applied MANIFEST.in exclude, global-exclude, recursive-exclude, and prune directives by matching compiled glob patterns against on-disk file names without Unicode normalization, so on macOS APFS or HFS+ an NFD file name could bypass an NFC exclusion rule and be packed into a source distribution. This issue is fixed in version 83.0.0."}]}, {"name": "shellingham", "version": "1.5.4", "vulns": []}, {"name": "sse-starlette", "version": "3.3.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "starlette", "version": "1.8.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "structlog", "version": "25.5.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "sympy", "version": "1.14.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "threadpoolctl", "version": "3.7.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "tokenizers", "version": "0.22.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "torch", "version": "2.14.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "tqdm", "version": "4.68.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "transformers", "version": "5.12.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "typer", "version": "0.26.7", "vulns": []}, {"name": "typing-inspection", "version": "0.4.2", "vulns": []}, {"name": "typing-extensions", "version": "4.15.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "uncalled-for", "version": "0.2.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "uvicorn", "version": "0.41.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "watchfiles", "version": "1.1.1", "vulns": []}, {"name": "websockets", "version": "16.0", "vulns": []}, {"name": "zipp", "version": "3.23.0", "vulns": []}], "fixes": []}
